  "answer": "{\"type\":\"selection\",\"packet_sha256\":\"e66f9bc5c8d3c38c171ce5f2b71ec8db539892c59cc816c1bd1f4cbb0dc9826\",\"batch_strategy\":\"Condition-response and failure-repair batch combining strong-composition endpoint probes, loading contrasts, local functional-group neighborhoods, and compact controls.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"0f06772820e6693753e3\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m211 tests whether endpoint growth continues beyond the measured condition range.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"44c8b389a6faf44f1f4c\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m59 probes a broad predicted endpoint regime in a heteroatom-containing scaffold.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"105457e008d11073c7b7\",\"reason\":\"High-composition m97 adds hydrophobic aromatic ester coverage and tests scaffold-specific endpoint growth.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"605436d35600502e8c2e\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m30 supplies an aromatic ketone control for testing whether endpoint expansion is chemically supported.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"f46da3c00b2199795e4c\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m169 probes whether a halogenated carbonyl-like scaffold can enter a delayed regime.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"0cf0d36290765378ae8d\",\"reason\":\"High-composition m114 with distinct loading probes loading and endpoint interaction in a polar aromatic ester.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"4862e2fb71344ce16021\",\"reason\":\"High-loading m177 tests whether a nitrobenzophenone-like scaffold retains a long endpoint after condition changes.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"f91285c618eacb53538b\",\"reason\":\"m200 at 2/1 and 150 uL probes loading response in a polar nitro alcohol family.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"3163a9b58f1a52a1992c\",\"reason\":\"High-composition m181 tests transfer of delayed endpoints across cyclic oxygen-containing carbonyl scaffolds.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"67fa39740fcf946a3154\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m98 tests whether a predicted aromatic ester tail is family-specific.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"0ac58929e586a4da4056\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m198 adds nitrobenzaldehyde-like endpoint coverage in a local aldehyde neighborhood.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"20913a7c2077b80b7351\",\"reason\":\"m120 with altered loading probes whether delayed alcohol-family behavior depends on sample amount.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"8f5452ff0e84ab2e2057\",\"reason\":\"m207 at higher loading tests loading dependence of a predicted delayed endpoint.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"596bd04bfe916866f908\",\"reason\":\"m128 changes loading in a sulfur-containing aromatic carbonyl family and tests transfer of high-response behavior.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"07a55cdab65b05f31561\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m82 probes a possible endpoint threshold in an acceptor-rich ester family.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"b29c3ac2de3ba2d8b5c9\",\"reason\":\"A second m82 loading condition separates loading effects from composition effects.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"c8324c0c30b89615c5fe\",\"reason\":\"m4 at strong composition continues an extended aromatic condition-response curve.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"00043aebb2540e369a7b\",\"reason\":\"Low-composition m125 anchors the compact side of a multifunctional aromatic response transition.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"780b13846ace50ede763\",\"reason\":\"Higher-composition m125 probes the upper side of that response transition at matched loading.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"b51a88b6dc4049704214\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m130 supplies a compact nitrile control in a high predicted endpoint region.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"4c15c048e4f33116df8d\",\"reason\":\"Low-composition m144 provides a second compact nitrile boundary control.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"34e3e4807176cfd57e57\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m126 tests whether a simple aromatic ether remains compact.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"c17fee6d4419cf961d3a\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m5 supplies a compact dihalogenated aromatic control.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"b33b7253147a64c9baeb\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m137 tests compact heavy-halogen behavior under a different loading condition.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"90b458cad40e4d8b82fd\",\"reason\":\"m157 provides a compact heavy-halogen control separating molecular weight from silica interaction.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"7f4bd7d11e89fe0d1d41\",\"reason\":\"Low-composition m113 adds a compact brominated anisole-like boundary point.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"4da6e3b93f29af1efa94\",\"reason\":\"m198 at moderate composition adds a local nitrobenzaldehyde response point.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"a04af55e394c31f4123a\",\"reason\":\"m192 at strong composition expands aromatic aldehyde and local carbonyl coverage.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"fe7d7af2c919facfe5f5\",\"reason\":\"m209 probes donor-acceptor and trifluoroether context in a phenol neighborhood.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"fefecd79dc057980f62c\",\"reason\":\"m81 probes a polar aromatic carbonyl or ester neighborhood with broad predicted V2 behavior.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"c096c324a71974b6ab37\",\"reason\":\"Strong-composition m34 at increased sample volume tests whether a weakly interacting halogenated aromatic develops a delayed tail.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null},{\"id\":\"a594ed374525b27ed662\",\"reason\":\"High-loading m186 probes loading sensitivity in a donor-containing brominated aromatic aldehyde family.\",\"hypothesis_id\":null}],\"hypotheses\":[],\"feedback_interpretation\":\"Measured feedback supports a separation between genuine long endpoints in polar or extended families and unsupported tails in compact aromatic, nitrile, and halogenated families. It also indicates that loading and solvent composition can interact with scaffold identity. The batch therefore emphasizes local response curves and compact controls.\",\"batch_rationale\":\"The batch combines strong-composition extrapolation points, loading contrasts, local aldehyde, ester, carbonyl, nitrile, sulfur, and heteroaromatic coverage, plus compact controls. It can repair endpoint underprediction in responsive families while limiting global tail correction through weakly interacting boundary examples. The resulting labels should improve Row-distribution generalization across solvent strength, loading, and local graph context.\"}",
